  "runtime_requirements": [
    "An index whose meta says norm = pt-1 is searched only with that rule, and US indexes (no norm key) only with the US rule.",
    "With PT-30.sqlite installed, every answer from an existing US index stays identical, including its Overture Maps credit.",
    "A PT address is written street first (ESTR MONUMENTAL 221), so a result names the house street first, keeps the register's spelling, and credits the index meta source.",
    "Only an exact house label matches: 222 never falls back to 221, a bare 11 never returns 11 B, and the house 13 never answers for the label 013A beside it.",
    "A label that is not a plain numeral ('5 1J', '11 B') is kept and matched in either case, so '5 1j' finds '5 1J'.",
    "The postcode is stored without the hyphen; a query types 9000-100, so the lookup strips the punctuation before comparing, as the US rule does.",
    "The detail line is the US join over what the row holds (city, PT-30, zip) — the register's city in its own spelling, upper case, sometimes with a municipality suffix ('SEIXAL PMZ'), occasionally empty."
  ]
}
